 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? That sounds lovely. Where are you off to? offline routes often mean smaller, quieter roads, so the traffic won't be as busy. That's the right choice. Try to take breaks in smaller towns along the way. That's the one. Park right outside and tell them you' be right back. Good plan. Go in, park the bike in the corridor, and find your friends. They' be relieved to see you back. Good to know. Either way, the green door is the way to go on a busy weekend.",
